Fetch a motor's thrust curve from ThrustCurve.org into the cache, so `hpr sim` flies it offline

Usage: hpr motors fetch [OPTIONS] <MOTOR>

Arguments:
  <MOTOR>
          The motor: its designation (F27R/L) or common name (F27), as ThrustCurve.org spells it

Options:
      --json
          Print one JSON document on standard output instead of text, errors included

      --manufacturer <MANUFACTURER>
          Its manufacturer, by name or abbreviation, where the name alone matches several motors

      --color <WHEN>
          When to use color. With auto, output to a terminal is colored, and NO_COLOR, FORCE_COLOR and CLICOLOR_FORCE are followed. JSON output never has color
          
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

      --file <ID>
          The ThrustCurve.org data file to take first, by its id, when the motor has it and it can be read. Otherwise the fetch takes the files in the usual order

      --offline
          Answer from the cache only, never the network

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Examples:
  Fetch a motor the bundled catalog lacks, so `hpr sim` flies it offline:
      hpr motors fetch F27
  Name its maker where the name alone matches several motors:
      hpr motors fetch G80 --manufacturer AeroTech

Guide: https://hpr.fusionspace.co/cli.html#motors-from-thrustcurveorg
